cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SqlToViz, please cite it as below. The software is pre-release alpha and its models are experimental and not human-validated."
title: "SqlToViz: chart recommendation from a SQL query and its result set"
type: software
version: "0.1.0-alpha.1"
# date-released: set when the first release is verified on all three registries (see docs/alpha-release.md)
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jmmana/sqltoviz"
url: "https://jmmana.github.io/sqltoviz/"
abstract: "SqlToViz recommends one of ten base chart classes (a table as fallback) from a SQL query and the rows it returned, with a frozen feature contract (SqlVizSpec-v1.0.0), deterministic semantic constraints and SDKs for Python, TypeScript and .NET. Bundled ONNX models are experimental candidates trained on synthetic and LLM-derived labels; no human validation exists yet."
keywords:
  - sql
  - data visualization
  - chart recommendation
  - onnx
  - text-to-sql
authors:
  - family-names: "Castillo Pinto"
    given-names: "Juan Manuel"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-5751-0709"
    # OWNER TODO: confirm the author list and order and add `affiliation:`.
    # Only the sole git committer was added automatically; add co-authors by hand (annotators/LLMs are not authors).
